      <h2>Common SST to EST Conversion Mistakes</h2>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Subtracting Instead of Adding</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">EST (UTC-5) is ahead of SST (UTC-11). You must add 6 hours to SST. Subtracting 6 hours yields UTC-17, which does not exist.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Missing Next-Day Rollover</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">SST times from 6:00 PM onward advance into the next calendar day in EST. Always check the date.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing Independent Samoa with American Samoa</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">Independent Samoa (Apia) uses UTC+13 (WST). American Samoa (Pago Pago) uses SST (UTC-11). Verify which Samoa you are scheduling for.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing EST with EDT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">EST is UTC-5 (winter). EDT is UTC-4 (summer). Using EST during summer introduces a 1-hour shift relative to New York local clocks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

